/P 103 0 R
/E (This table outlines the cryptographic parameters used in ChromaSafe's symmetric encryption implementation. AES-256 with Galois/Counter Mode \(GCM\) provides authenticated encryption, ensuring both confidentiality and integrity protection. The 256-bit key size offers military-grade security, while GCM mode automatically detects any tampering with encrypted data through authentication tags. The 96-bit initialization vector \(IV\) is NIST-recommended for GCM implementations, and the 128-bit authentication tag provides strong integrity verification.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [0]
>>
